WEBVTT

01:30.270 --> 01:32.480
Episode 9: Sweet Memory (Part 1)

01:33.280 --> 01:38.550
What do you mean, I knew
 I was going to be kidnapped?

01:42.190 --> 01:43.640
Here you are.

01:43.640 --> 01:46.240
Your summer tropical parfaits.

01:47.290 --> 01:51.780
I can see why this was in the top spot 
on Osanai Sweets Selection: Summer.

01:49.380 --> 01:51.750
Osanai's Top 10!

01:59.360 --> 02:03.030
A certain level of resolve 
is required to order this parfait.

02:03.490 --> 02:07.070
You need an empty stomach 
and your desire dialed up to 11,

02:07.070 --> 02:09.020
then you just <i>go</i> for it.

02:09.720 --> 02:15.240
I had a rough time the other day, 
so it's the perfect way to reward myself.

02:15.620 --> 02:19.930
The trick is to eat the watermelon first, 
as it doesn't go well with the whipped cream.

02:29.070 --> 02:30.670
Sorry.

02:31.040 --> 02:33.190
You were in the middle of saying something.

02:33.470 --> 02:35.580
Right, yeah.

02:39.110 --> 02:44.990
My friend, Dojima Kengo, 
was being a meddler this summer.

02:46.130 --> 02:51.200
A second-year high schooler named Kawamata 
Sanae had gotten involved with a bad group.

02:51.200 --> 02:54.330
Kengo was asked by 
Sanae-san's sister, Kasumi-san,

02:54.330 --> 02:57.590
to help her older sister leave the group.

02:58.110 --> 03:02.500
But the leader of this group 
turned out to be rather volatile,

03:02.500 --> 03:04.850
and Sanae-san was paralyzed with fear.

03:05.790 --> 03:08.120
Kengo was helpless to do anything.

03:09.210 --> 03:12.560
That leader's name was Isawa Hasemi.

03:13.390 --> 03:19.260
And the leader of the group that 
kidnapped you was also an Isawa Hasemi.

03:19.690 --> 03:21.300
Surprising, huh?

03:21.300 --> 03:22.760
Isn't it?

03:23.450 --> 03:27.320
Can you believe how good 
this melon is for the price?

03:27.320 --> 03:29.150
It really is surprising.

03:35.310 --> 03:37.700
Something's bothering me.

03:38.700 --> 03:42.320
Why was Kengo there that day?

03:42.990 --> 03:45.840
He told me very clearly...

03:45.840 --> 03:48.840
that he was staking out 
a group of drug abusers.

03:48.840 --> 03:52.120
It goes without saying that
 he meant Isawa-san's group.

03:52.800 --> 03:55.860
Now, why was I there that day?

03:56.360 --> 04:01.310
I was by the station because 
you'd asked me to come to Berry Berry.

04:02.180 --> 04:04.790
I went into the shop 
because I was getting hungry.

04:05.260 --> 04:08.090
I met you there, too.

04:08.740 --> 04:11.210
Why were you there that day?

04:11.760 --> 04:15.390
Isawa-san and I know each other.

04:15.390 --> 04:17.760
We both attended Takaba Middle School.

04:18.310 --> 04:20.120
She's a bad girl.

04:20.120 --> 04:21.510
I knew that.

04:22.260 --> 04:24.260
Anyway, go on.

04:24.610 --> 04:26.360
You haven't answered my question.

04:27.050 --> 04:29.490
It's fine. It doesn't bother me.

04:33.920 --> 04:37.850
Osanai-san, did you pick out that dress
 to match the tropical parfait?

04:38.650 --> 04:39.610
Does it work?

04:39.610 --> 04:40.520
Pretty well.

04:40.520 --> 04:41.930
I appreciate it.

04:42.330 --> 04:46.230
But your outfit when you got 
kidnapped worked even better.

04:47.200 --> 04:49.890
Or rather, it was familiar.

04:52.560 --> 04:55.320
Hi, sorry, could I get a tea?

04:56.050 --> 04:58.960
Whenever you're out 
in town on the weekends,

04:58.960 --> 05:02.530
you're usually dressed in 
a way that's not like you.

05:03.050 --> 05:05.910
Seemingly to avoid anyone noticing 
that you're Osanai Yuki.

05:06.390 --> 05:12.220
But that day, your outfit closely resembled 
Funato High's summer uniform.

05:13.050 --> 05:20.670
Anyone who only knew you from school 
would have recognized you instantly.

05:21.920 --> 05:26.970
I was really unlucky, 
getting kidnapped on such a day.

05:28.560 --> 05:29.690
You were.

05:33.670 --> 05:39.250
So having been kidnapped, 
you sent me an SOS message.

05:40.150 --> 05:48.000
You obfuscated the message 
so your kidnappers wouldn't figure it out.

05:49.030 --> 05:52.760
They might've done something bad 
if they found out you tried to call for help.

05:53.120 --> 05:57.040
And they might've still thought to
 take you elsewhere, as thick as they were.

05:59.030 --> 06:00.270
That was my thinking.

06:06.280 --> 06:10.940
But when we found the car at Nanbu 
Gymnasium, I knew something was wrong.

06:11.780 --> 06:16.060
The front passenger seat was a mess, 
meaning you must've been in the rear.

06:16.680 --> 06:20.420
If they'd tied you up, you wouldn't 
have been able to send a text message.

06:20.850 --> 06:24.330
You also couldn't have done so
with someone sitting next to you.

06:25.450 --> 06:29.720
And yet, the message you sent me...

06:29.700 --> 06:32.200
I'm sorry

06:29.700 --> 06:32.200
Please buy four candy apples and a canelé

06:29.700 --> 06:32.200
I'm sorry

06:35.490 --> 06:38.160
It seems implausible 
you could've discreetly typed

06:38.750 --> 06:43.360
such a long message
 while being transported.

06:43.830 --> 06:47.610
I type really fast.

06:47.610 --> 06:51.630
And Isawa-san and the others 
were very careless.

06:52.530 --> 06:53.730
That's hard to believe.

06:55.200 --> 06:59.770
You left home that day 
knowing I would be coming over.

07:00.720 --> 07:05.520
The ransom call was made
 a little after 1:30.

07:05.520 --> 07:08.220
That leaves a 90-minute gap.

07:09.630 --> 07:14.870
So, Osanai-san, what were you doing 
from 12 to 1:30, and where?

07:14.870 --> 07:17.350
A girl must have her secrets.

07:18.130 --> 07:20.460
And I'm trying to expose those secrets.

07:20.940 --> 07:24.320
Though that's not a very 
classy thing to do, admittedly.

07:38.870 --> 07:39.890
Hey...

07:39.890 --> 07:41.890
Do you still have more to say?

07:42.420 --> 07:43.670
Only if you want me to.

07:44.240 --> 07:45.940
You're such a liar.

07:45.940 --> 07:48.160
You have no intention of stopping.

07:48.430 --> 07:49.850
Here you go.

07:52.950 --> 07:56.220
There are things about your actions 
that leave me with questions.

07:56.960 --> 08:01.070
And your connections are 
too perfect to be coincidence.

08:02.450 --> 08:07.760
More than that, though...
There's something I find strange.

08:08.290 --> 08:13.070
Why did I drag you out on a sweets tour?

08:13.710 --> 08:16.730
That's the part you're not sure about, isn't it?

08:17.800 --> 08:18.810
Osanai's Top 10!

08:19.350 --> 08:22.970
When you gave me this map, you said:

08:23.610 --> 08:26.580
"This here is going to determine
 my destiny this summer."

08:27.190 --> 08:29.520
And it really did.

08:30.550 --> 08:37.760
From this map, I deciphered your 
message and managed to save you.

08:40.280 --> 08:41.970
Was it a coincidence?

08:42.380 --> 08:47.540
I have that map completely memorized, 
so it was the first thing that came to mind

08:47.540 --> 08:50.600
when I needed to fake 
a message asking you for help.

08:50.590 --> 08:51.460
Osanai's Top 10!

08:51.240 --> 08:55.790
That day, I said I'd buy you 
the next thing on this list.

08:51.460 --> 08:51.590
Osanai's Top 10!

08:56.570 --> 09:00.990
Needless to say, that meant the 
candy apples from Muramatsuya.

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Osanai's Top 10!

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Cecilia

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Summer Tropical Parfait

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Tinker Linker

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Peach Pie

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Muramatsuya

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
Candy Apples

08:58.850 --> 09:03.230
*Note sale date!*

09:01.650 --> 09:03.230
And yet, you said:

09:03.230 --> 09:05.490
Tinker Linker's peach pie!

09:05.820 --> 09:08.250
You didn't even hesitate when you said it.

09:08.730 --> 09:11.400
And that's because you'd 
already eaten a candy apple

09:11.400 --> 09:13.450
when you left before noon that day.

09:14.380 --> 09:18.100
You planned to eat 
those candy apples with me.

09:18.100 --> 09:20.610
So why did you go on ahead?

09:21.310 --> 09:25.900
Because you knew you 
were going to be kidnapped.

09:26.810 --> 09:29.320
You knew since the first day of summer,

09:29.320 --> 09:34.100
when you handed me
 the Osanai Sweets Selection: Summer.

09:39.760 --> 09:43.870
You took action because you knew 
you were going to be kidnapped.

09:44.610 --> 09:48.880
The Osanai Sweets Selection: Summer 
was your way of preparing.

09:50.700 --> 09:57.600
You used this map to 
take me all across Kira City.

09:59.330 --> 10:00.670
It was all delicious.

10:01.280 --> 10:05.210
The watermelon frozen yogurt, 
the green tea shaved ice...

10:05.210 --> 10:08.400
And most of all, 
those Charlottes were divine.

10:09.600 --> 10:13.400
But the sweet treats 
weren't the true purpose.

10:14.010 --> 10:16.920
By having me follow a map the way you did,

10:16.920 --> 10:22.040
you were putting it all in my head

10:22.040 --> 10:26.050
and priming me to recall it 
as soon as you needed me to.

10:27.640 --> 10:29.810
I totally let you train me.

10:30.430 --> 10:32.800
When we passed Muramatsuya,

10:32.800 --> 10:37.520
I asked about their candy apples
 being in your rankings.

10:32.810 --> 10:34.440
<b>Muramatsuya</b>

10:37.520 --> 10:39.480
You seemed happy I did.

10:40.260 --> 10:46.150
When I realized the note left by Kengo
 in the fast-food joint was a map,

10:46.150 --> 10:48.820
you were absolutely ecstatic.

10:50.140 --> 10:51.780
You got me good.

10:52.330 --> 10:55.090
I admit I'm disappointed in myself
 for letting you best me.

10:55.700 --> 10:57.580
But never mind that.

10:57.580 --> 10:59.340
Why didn't you tell me?

10:59.940 --> 11:04.370
You were being targeted over an old grudge,
 and knew you might be kidnapped.

11:04.370 --> 11:06.720
You could've just asked me for help.

11:06.720 --> 11:09.720
Didn't it cross your mind 
what might happen if things went south?

11:10.300 --> 11:13.010
Didn't you even once 
consider how I would feel?

11:19.900 --> 11:20.920
Sorry.

11:25.500 --> 11:27.780
You're right, Kobato-kun.

11:27.780 --> 11:30.590
I had a candy apple.

11:31.750 --> 11:37.670
I knew since before summer break started
that Isawa-san was likely going to kidnap me.

11:37.670 --> 11:41.720
And I'd decided to have you help me.

11:42.620 --> 11:47.800
But I knew if Isawa-san found out I'd spoken up,

11:47.800 --> 11:49.870
you might end up in real trouble.

11:51.810 --> 11:55.500
I thought Dojima-kun might come, too.

11:55.500 --> 12:00.780
I figured he'd be the only one
 you could depend on.

12:02.040 --> 12:04.300
It turned out exactly that way,

12:04.300 --> 12:07.270
though I never expected a fight to break out.

12:08.060 --> 12:10.400
Dojima-kun got injured.

12:10.400 --> 12:12.610
And you ended up getting hurt, too.

12:13.300 --> 12:16.280
I do want to apologize for that, too.

12:16.280 --> 12:18.290
It doesn't really bother me.

12:19.220 --> 12:22.790
But could you tell me what happened 
between you and Isawa Hasemi?

12:25.920 --> 12:29.100
Sorry. I don't like talking about it.

12:29.100 --> 12:30.530
It's in the past.

12:32.590 --> 12:33.940
What's wrong?

12:35.110 --> 12:36.050
Nothing.

12:37.260 --> 12:38.530
You're right.

12:38.990 --> 12:40.410
You shouldn't accept it.

12:40.850 --> 12:45.010
I should probably have asked you 
for help from the very beginning.

13:05.420 --> 13:06.610
I see.

13:08.240 --> 13:10.190
I knew there'd be one more thing.

13:17.920 --> 13:19.050
Osanai-san.

13:20.230 --> 13:23.040
I'm still stunned by your 
willingness to take action.

13:23.500 --> 13:28.150
I find that I tend to stay put and think.

13:28.800 --> 13:31.310
I'm constantly reminded 
that I'm no match for you.

13:34.850 --> 13:39.830
This whole summer, we've been 
going out to get sweets together.

13:40.370 --> 13:43.910
Yet you knew about the 
kidnapping plot all along.

13:44.840 --> 13:46.960
You knew precisely when it would happen.

13:47.660 --> 13:49.590
You know what that means?

13:53.140 --> 13:54.340
You had an insider.

14:00.600 --> 14:02.210
Your mother said to me:

14:02.770 --> 14:08.270
She seems to be on the phone a lot
at night since summer break started.

14:08.270 --> 14:11.480
I was sure she'd found a good friend.

14:12.080 --> 14:14.430
There was no way you would've trained me

14:14.430 --> 14:18.230
as a simple defensive measure
 against Isawa-san,

14:18.860 --> 14:24.190
who was about to cause you harm, 
after you'd gained inside knowledge.

14:24.980 --> 14:27.310
You'd no doubt come up 
with a way to retaliate.

14:28.460 --> 14:29.450
Am I wrong?

14:32.000 --> 14:35.180
Having established an insider,

14:35.180 --> 14:39.470
you would've promoted the idea of the 
Osanai Yuki kidnapping plot within the group,

14:40.040 --> 14:42.360
and controlled every aspect, even the day.

14:42.960 --> 14:45.020
You'd also prepare a rescuer.

14:45.890 --> 14:47.780
What would become of Isawa Hasemi?

14:48.550 --> 14:52.650
Assault, drug abuse, and kidnapping.

14:54.360 --> 14:56.610
She wouldn't be let off with probation.

14:57.090 --> 15:02.420
Which means juvenile detention, 
or potentially even jail time.

15:03.200 --> 15:10.710
Your ultimate objective was Isawa Hasemi's 
arrest and prosecution for kidnapping.

15:32.280 --> 15:34.140
I should have expected no less.

15:35.120 --> 15:39.220
You don't proclaim so pretentiously 
to <i>want to be</i> ordinary for nothing.

15:41.870 --> 15:46.370
Anyone else would have failed 
to figure me out so fully.

15:46.990 --> 15:51.120
I always think about 
how talented you are, too.

15:51.590 --> 15:57.680
I could never make such 
deep deductions the way you do.

15:58.850 --> 16:01.600
So you admit it, then?

16:02.020 --> 16:06.720
You were the one who got
Isawa-san to kidnap you.

16:07.130 --> 16:07.970
No.

16:09.630 --> 16:11.670
Let me introduce you to my guest.

16:11.670 --> 16:13.050
Just a second.

16:16.640 --> 16:17.890
Okay, come in.

16:36.810 --> 16:38.990
Is this the crazy guy 
you were talking about?

16:38.990 --> 16:40.010
Yeah.

16:40.010 --> 16:42.810
We talked it over, though.

16:42.810 --> 16:45.510
Okay. Fine, then.

16:45.510 --> 16:46.520
Let me introduce you.

16:47.190 --> 16:49.160
This is my acquaintance, Kobato-kun.

16:50.110 --> 16:53.530
I caused him a lot of 
trouble with our project.

16:54.210 --> 16:57.060
Kobato-kun, this is Kawamata-san.

16:57.060 --> 17:00.140
Wait, Yuki! I never said 
you could tell him my name!

17:00.610 --> 17:03.770
Anyway, make sure you get rid of this.

17:06.750 --> 17:10.040
We don't know each other anymore, okay?

17:10.950 --> 17:12.320
I know.

17:12.820 --> 17:15.620
Bye, Sanae. I'll be praying for your safety.

17:30.930 --> 17:34.220
Let me explain, Kobato-kun. So—

17:34.220 --> 17:35.250
Hold it.

17:36.520 --> 17:39.940
You're right. I had an insider.

17:41.040 --> 17:45.420
Otherwise, I couldn't have been 
kidnapped in such a specific way.

17:46.510 --> 17:48.470
She was very useful to me.

17:49.570 --> 17:52.000
Sanae-san threatened me.

17:52.870 --> 17:55.750
She said Isawa-san despised me,

17:56.180 --> 18:01.000
and she was going to capture me this 
summer break and teach me a lesson.

18:02.460 --> 18:06.600
I helped Sanae-san during middle school.

18:07.330 --> 18:11.740
Isawa-san and the others 
were taken into custody as a result.

18:11.740 --> 18:14.570
Sanae-san managed to leave the group.

18:15.560 --> 18:22.530
But once her probation was over, 
Isawa-san started looking for the insider.

18:22.890 --> 18:25.520
And Sanae-san immediately 
sucked up to Isawa-san.

18:26.530 --> 18:31.080
And once Isawa-san started suspecting her,
 she began threatening me.

18:32.050 --> 18:35.720
She demanded that 
I help her to get out again.

18:35.720 --> 18:40.330
If I refused, she would 
hand me over to Isawa-san.

18:41.300 --> 18:46.550
Sooner or later, they would have figured out
 that I was involved in Sanae-san's rescue.

18:46.890 --> 18:51.590
That's why I got her to work for me.

18:53.860 --> 18:58.530
I'm sure you know what's 
in here now, don't you?

19:02.530 --> 19:11.460
I was under the assumption that Isawa-san
used a voice changer to make the ransom call.

19:12.060 --> 19:14.200
That's what your mother said, too.

19:14.740 --> 19:18.020
They want five million in exchange for her.

19:18.020 --> 19:20.460
It was a strange modulated voice.

19:21.030 --> 19:25.790
But in order to get the ransom money, 
they would have needed to call again.

19:26.790 --> 19:30.940
Yet, the voice changer was 
left abandoned in the car.

19:32.340 --> 19:37.270
What point are you trying
 to make, Kobato-kun?

19:37.920 --> 19:40.660
The voice changer was a fake,

19:40.660 --> 19:43.990
used to make it look like Isawa-san 
and her group were behind it.

19:46.110 --> 19:48.650
They weren't the ones 
who made the ransom call.

19:49.560 --> 19:50.970
It was Kawamata Sanae.

19:54.210 --> 19:56.260
<i>This is Osanai Yuki's home, isn't it?</i>

19:56.780 --> 19:58.680
<i>Just shut up and listen.</i>

19:59.620 --> 20:01.610
<i>I'm only going to say this once.</i>

20:02.410 --> 20:05.760
<i>Your daughter's been a real pain in the ass.</i>

20:06.390 --> 20:09.290
<i>So we've kidnapped her.</i>

20:09.830 --> 20:12.970
<i>We'll give her back in exchange 
for five million yen.</i>

20:13.660 --> 20:16.510
<i>Got it? I'll call again.</i>

20:19.940 --> 20:23.640
We planned a script and 
recorded it ahead of time.

20:25.210 --> 20:29.220
I couldn't have her panicking 
and running her mouth.

20:31.150 --> 20:35.660
With that pretense, 
I had Sanae-san say all that.

20:36.620 --> 20:38.560
Poor Sanae-san.

20:38.560 --> 20:41.680
And she even gave this to me.

20:42.480 --> 20:45.090
In other words...

20:45.610 --> 20:52.280
You weren't satisfied with Isawa Hasemi 
being arrested for kidnapping and detention.

20:52.990 --> 20:58.230
So you upgraded it to 
a kidnapping for ransom.

20:59.730 --> 21:04.450
You were the one who kidnapped yourself.

21:04.450 --> 21:05.770
That's right.

21:06.330 --> 21:08.950
You finally worked it out, Kobato-kun.
